---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Events & Opportunities | Cardiac Arrest Research Hub"
  description="Conferences, working groups, and collaboration opportunities relevant to cardiac arrest survivorship research."
>
  <div class="content-page events-page mx-auto max-w-5xl space-y-14 px-6 py-12 lg:px-8">
    <section class="content-hero space-y-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        Upcoming Events and Opportunities to get involved
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200">
        In this page we aim to bring together conferences, networks, and project collaboration
        opportunities that can strengthen cardiac arrest survivorship research.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        Conferences &amp; Congresses
      </h2>
      <div
        class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900"
      >
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Events at a glance</h3>
        <table class="mt-3 w-full min-w-[460px] text-sm">
          <thead class="text-left text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-300">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-2 py-2 font-medium">Event</th>
              <th class="px-2 py-2 font-medium">Dates and location</th>
              <th class="px-2 py-2 font-medium">About the event</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 align-top">
              <td class="px-2 py-2 font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                <a
                  class="text-teal-700 hover:text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-300"
                  href="https://suddencardiacarrestuk.org/life-without-limits/"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noreferrer">Life Without Limits — SCA UK National Conference</a
                >
              </td>
              <td class="px-2 py-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200"
                ><strong>15 May 2027</strong><br />Hinckley, UK; welcome evening 14 May</td
              >
              <td class="px-2 py-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200"
                >A national gathering for cardiac arrest survivors, co-survivors, rescuers and
                healthcare professionals, with expert speakers, shared experiences and opportunities
                to connect.</td
              >
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 align-top">
              <td class="px-2 py-2 font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                <a
                  class="text-teal-700 hover:text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-300"
                  href="https://sparkoflife.au/"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noreferrer">Spark of Life 2027</a
                >
              </td>
              <td class="px-2 py-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200"
                ><strong>13–15 May 2027</strong><br />Adelaide, Australia</td
              >
              <td class="px-2 py-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200"
                >The Australian Resuscitation Council conference brings together researchers,
                clinicians, educators and community advocates to explore resuscitation and
                post-cardiac arrest recovery.</td
              >
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 align-top">
              <td class="px-2 py-2 font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                <a
                  class="text-teal-700 hover:text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-300"
                  href="https://www.erc.edu/events/congress/general-information/"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noreferrer">ERC Congress — Resuscitation 2027</a
                >
              </td>
              <td class="px-2 py-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200"
                ><strong>30 September–2 October 2027</strong><br />Scottish Event Campus, Glasgow,
                UK</td
              >
              <td class="px-2 py-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200"
                >The European Resuscitation Council’s annual congress brings together the
                international resuscitation community to share research, clinical developments and
                approaches to improving care.</td
              >
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 align-top">
              <td class="px-2 py-2 font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                <a
                  class="text-teal-700 hover:text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-300"
                  href="https://professional.heart.org/en/meetings/resuscitation-science-symposium/registration-and-housing"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noreferrer">AHA Resuscitation Science Symposium 2027</a
                >
              </td>
              <td class="px-2 py-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200"
                ><strong>6–7 November 2027</strong><br />Boston, USA</td
              >
              <td class="px-2 py-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200"
                >An international forum for resuscitation research, connecting basic, clinical and
                community-based science with advances in cardiac arrest care.</td
              >
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 align-top">
              <td class="px-2 py-2 font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                <a
                  class="text-teal-700 hover:text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-300"
                  href="https://www.citizencprsummit.org/"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noreferrer">Cardiac Arrest Survival Summit 2027</a
                >
              </td>
              <td class="px-2 py-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200"
                ><strong>30 November–4 December 2027</strong><br />Arizona Grand Resort, USA</td
              >
              <td class="px-2 py-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200"
                >A multidisciplinary gathering of researchers, healthcare professionals, survivors,
                rescuers and advocates working to strengthen the chain of survival.</td
              >
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        Networks &amp; Working Groups
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <article
          class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">COST Action CA24142</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200">
            COST Action CA24142 - <strong
              >Precision Medicine for Cardiac Arrest (PREMEDICARE)</strong
            >. This is a Europe-wide networking framework that can support exchange, mobility, and
            coordinated action. Includes a focus on understanding the long-term burden of OHCA in
            the young.
          </p>
          <a
            class="mt-3 inline-flex text-sm font-medium text-teal-700 transition hover:text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-300"
            href="https://www.cost.eu/actions/CA24142/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >
            Visit COST Action page →
          </a>
        </article>

        <article
          class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            SABRE: Support After Bystander Resuscitation
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200">
            The SABRE network is an international collaboration established in 2024 to strengthen
            support services for people who have attempted CPR during an out-of-hospital cardiac
            arrest. The network meets every three months online, and in person at conferences, to
            share knowledge, collaborate and support the formation of bystander support services.
            All are welcome to join.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200">
            Please contact <a
              class="font-medium text-teal-700 hover:text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-300"
              href="mailto:vicky.joshi@gcu.ac.uk">Vicky.joshi@gcu.ac.uk</a
            > if you would like to be included in the SABRE mailing list.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        Projects Seeking Collaborators
      </h2>
      <div
        class="rounded-2xl border border-dashed border-slate-300 bg-white p-6 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900"
      >
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200">
          This section is intentionally drafted as a placeholder for projects that are actively
          looking for partners (e.g., clinical sites, qualitative researchers, patient/public
          involvement contributors, data science support, and implementation partners).
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-200">
          Proposed format for each listing: project title, collaboration need, timeline, country or
          region, and contact link.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
